 "reference_time_robustness_note": "onset_reference_time_robustness.csv: five reference-time conventions for 'the clones' click counts differ'. Under ALL five the onset/ridge ratio is NON-CONSTANT across s_d and rises from s_d=0.0025 to 0.04 (window 0.18->1.10->1.28; full-run-to-fixation 0.08->0.24->0.21; at-neutral-median-time 0.12->0.44->0.42; at-half-own-T_end 0.50->1.78->1.62; p_click 0.18->1.09->1.28), so 'onset tracks ridge' fails under every convention. The SIGN reversal (onset crossing to above the ridge at s_d=0.04) holds under 3 of 5 conventions (window, p_click, half-own-T_end); under the two conventions that count more accumulated clicks (full run, fixed absolute time = neutral median T_fix) the onset stays below the ridge at all three s_d, with the ratio still rising 2.6x-3.7x from s_d=0.0025 to 0.04.",
