 "mechanism_diagnostic": "Diagnostics interpolated (log-x) at the FINAL crossings from the per-rung table. At the T_fix ridge: s_d=0.0025 (U/s=0.94): |Delta<k>| = 1.82 hits, s_d*|Delta<k>| = 0.0045, mean clicks/clone = 3.30, frac runs with unequal clicks = 0.96; s_d=0.01 (U/s=0.40): 0.55 hits, 0.0055, 0.21 clicks/clone, 0.41; s_d=0.04 (U/s=0.64): 0.34 hits, 0.0137, 0.02 clicks/clone, 0.05. So at weak s_d the strict ratchet has clicked ~3 times per clone and 96% of runs already differ in click count BEFORE the T_fix ridge is reached (one click costs only 0.25%), whereas at strong s_d the ridge is crossed with essentially zero clicks (5% of runs differ) on a sub-click mean-load gap (0.34 hits x 4% = 1.4% fitness gap). The window fitness gap s_d*|Delta<k>| at the ridge varies x3 (0.0045-0.0137) across a x16 range of s_d, i.e. it is less variable than the click statistic (whose crossing moves x4.8 in U_d/s_d) but is not an invariant.",
